.TH SENTINEL 1 "November 2026" "Sentinel 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sentinel \- local-first Linux security events and system health monitor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sentinel
.RI [ command ]
.br
.B sentinel
.B --help
.br
.B sentinel
.B -update
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sentinel
collects events from available local logging sources, applies deterministic
explanation rules, correlates repeated authentication events, stores history
in a local SQLite database, and provides a terminal user interface.
.PP
Findings are heuristic explanations of log patterns. They are not proof of
compromise and Sentinel is not an antivirus, firewall, SIEM, or intrusion
prevention system.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B sentinel
Start the Textual terminal interface.
.TP
.B sentinel check
Print system, dependency, and source capability information as JSON.
.TP
.B sentinel events
Analyze and print recent findings.
.TP
.B sentinel events -n LIMIT
Analyze up to LIMIT events. The value is clamped to the range 1 through 2000.
.TP
.B sentinel export json [FILE]
Write a JSON report. The default destination is ~/sentinel-report.json.
.TP
.B sentinel export html [FILE]
Write a standalone HTML report. The default destination is ~/sentinel-report.html.
.TP
.B sentinel version
Print the installed version.
.TP
.B sentinel update
Update an installation made with the GitHub installer. RPM-managed installations
are directed to the system package manager. If RPM ownership cannot be verified,
the update is stopped.
.TP
.B sentinel --help
Show command-line help.
.SH DATA AND PRIVACY
Sentinel processes events locally. It does not send telemetry, logs, reports,
or configuration to a server. Event history is stored in a local SQLite
database under the user's XDG data directory. Configuration is stored under
the user's XDG config directory.
.PP
Logs may contain usernames, hostnames, IP addresses, command arguments, and
file paths. Review and redact reports before sharing them.
.SH SECURITY
Run Sentinel as an ordinary user. It does not automatically request root
privileges, modify source logs, change firewall or security policies, block
processes, or automatically remediate findings.
.PP
Sentinel invokes fixed system utilities where needed and does not execute
commands derived from log messages.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/sentinel/config.json
User configuration, unless XDG_CONFIG_HOME is set.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/sentinel/events.sqlite3
Local event history, unless XDG_DATA_HOME is set.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/sentinel/venv
Dedicated environment used by the GitHub installer, unless XDG_DATA_HOME is set.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Override the base directory for user configuration.
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Override the base directory for application data.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR dnf (8)
